5. Important Annotations in Spring Boot

Stereotype Annotations (marking beans)

@Component → generic component.

@Service → service layer.

@Repository → persistence/DAO layer.

@Controller → handles web requests (MVC).

@RestController → @Controller + @ResponseBody.


Bean & Config Annotations

@Bean → explicitly define a bean.

@Configuration → marks a class that provides beans.

@Value → inject values from properties.

@PropertySource → load external property files.


Dependency Injection Annotations

@Autowired → injects dependencies.

@Qualifier → specify bean when multiple exist.

@Primary → default bean when multiple candidates.


Boot-Specific

@SpringBootApplication → main entry point (combines @Configuration, @EnableAutoConfiguration, @ComponentScan).

@EnableAutoConfiguration → triggers auto-configuration.

@ComponentScan → scans for beans in packages.



