6. REST & Endpoints

Web Services

Definition: Communication mechanism between two applications over a network.


REST (Representational State Transfer)

Uses HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE).

Data formats → JSON, XML.


REST in Spring Boot

@RestController → defines REST endpoints.

@GetMapping, @PostMapping, @PutMapping, @DeleteMapping → HTTP mappings.

ResponseEntity → build custom responses.



---

7. Spring Boot Features

1. Spring Boot Starter

Predefined set of dependencies.

Examples:

spring-boot-starter-web → build web apps.

spring-boot-starter-data-jpa → database access.

spring-boot-starter-test → testing.




2. Actuator

Provides production-ready features.

Endpoints like /actuator/health, /actuator/metrics.



3. Build & Packaging

Uses Maven/Gradle for build.

Produces JAR/WAR with embedded server.





---

8. Maven Basics (since Spring Boot is Maven-heavy)

pom.xml → Project Object Model (dependencies, plugins, build config).

Maven lifecycle: clean → compile → test → package → install → deploy.

Maven Wrapper → ensures correct Maven version across systems.



